        "command" : "look",
        "forcings" : [

        ],
        "id" : "07FDCC3D-C0B7-4CF5-B10C-525F17304CD8",
        "locked" : false,
        "origin" : "author",
        "output" : "Iron Gates\nWrought-iron gates stand open on one hinge apiece, rust freckling the scrollwork. The gravel drive runs north toward the dark shape of the house.",
        "tags" : [

        ]
      },
      {
        "blessing" : {
          "output" : "Gravel Drive\nThe drive curves between bare lime trees, gravel crunching underfoot. The house looms ahead to the north; the gates are back south.\n\nYou can see Tobias here.\n\nFar off in the village, the church bell counts another quarter hour gone.",
          "scope" : "this-thread"
        },
        "children" : [
          {
            "blessing" : {
              "output" : "Fountain Court\nA paved court before the front door, holding a dry fountain crusted with last summer's leaves. The greenhouse glimmers palely to the west; a squat brick shed hunches to the east; the front door of the house is north.\n\nThe wind comes off the downs and worries at the bare limes.",
              "scope" : "this-thread"
            },
            "children" : [
              {
                "blessing" : {
                  "output" : "Entrance Hall\nThe heart of the house: a cold marble floor, a dead fireplace under a wide mantel, and a tall case clock standing silent against the stairs. Doors lead west to the study and east to the kitchen; a colder passage runs north.\n\nYou can see a grey overcoat and Mrs Kettle here.\n\nYou step out of the wind, and your ears sing in the sudden quiet.\n\nThe house holds its old hush — mothballs, cold ash, and wax.\n\nMrs Kettle blocks your way!",
                  "scope" : "this-thread"
                },
                "children" : [
                  {
                    "blessing" : {
                      "output" : "The housekeeper, planted before the study door with her knitting and no intention of moving. Her eyes say the study is not for visitors.",
                      "scope" : "this-thread"
                    },
                    "children" : [
                      {
                        "blessing" : {
                          "output" : "Mrs Kettle does not move from the study door. \"The study is not for visitors,\" she says, to her knitting.",
                          "scope" : "this-thread"
                        },
                        "children" : [
                          {
                            "blessing" : {
                              "output" : "Kitchen\nCopper pans hang in ranks over the cold range. The pantry door stands in the north wall.\n\nYou can see a garden shears and a sherry bottle here.\n\nThe Smoke follows you.",
                              "scope" : "this-thread"
                            },
